  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It builds the forest from three instanced draws plus a ground plane: 8,000 trunks, 8,000 cone canopies (8,000 trees) and 2,000 rocks. A fixed-seed LCG places everything, so the layout is the same on every load. Canopies and rocks get per-instance HSL colours. The scene has one shadow-casting directional light, exponential fog (`effects.fog` with `mode: \"exp\"`), and a hemisphere light and neutral environment for fill. The camera orbits slowly at radius 100 and height 62 via `app.camera?.setPose` in `onFrame`. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after the first frame. `typecheck` passes. I haven't run `vite build` or rendered the scene in a browser, so I haven't seen the shadows, fog density or framing.",
